Description: V3D register and counter module for vc4top (DKMS)
 vc4mon is a small out-of-tree kernel module that exposes the VideoCore IV
 (V3D) register block under /sys/kernel/vc4mon/, so an unprivileged vc4top
 can read the same registers without /dev/mem and sample the performance
 counters through two write-only files.
 .
 The module does not register a platform driver, does not bind or unbind
 vc4_v3d and does not request_mem_region().  ident/regs/perf are read-only
 0444; perf_enable (PCTRE) and perf_clear (PCTRC) are the only writable
 files.  A udev helper grants group vc4 write-only access to those two.
 .
 Source is installed in /usr/src/vc4top-1.0.4 and built for the running
 kernel with DKMS.  Kernel upgrades rebuild it automatically at boot once
 the matching kernel headers are present.

